From 122abb763c2fd085ab6e7d280ac25fcfdfe17c86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:02:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/41] firmware: qcom: scm: report the qseecom paths that
 leave TZ parked

Two error paths gave up on a listener request without saying what that costs.
An out-of-range listener id returned -EINVAL and said nothing, though it leaves
the application parked exactly like the unexpected-response-type case next to
it, which does explain itself; report it and use -EPROTO to match. And the
give-up answer at the end of the round limit had its return value dropped, so a
failure to deliver it left the wedge the answer exists to prevent, silently.

No functional change beyond the errno, which no caller distinguishes.

Reported-by: Kimi K3
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index c30cdd639..9c25ebac6 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2193,8 +2193,18 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_service_listeners(struct qcom_scm_qseecom_resp *res)
 			return -EPROTO;
 		}
 
-		if (res->data > U32_MAX)
-			return -EINVAL;
+		if (res->data > U32_MAX) {
+			/*
+			 * A listener id that does not fit one. There is
+			 * nothing to answer -- responding needs a valid id --
+			 * so the application stays parked and the interface is
+			 * stuck until reboot, same as the case above.
+			 */
+			dev_err(__scm->dev,
+				"qseecom: listener id %llx out of range; the interface is now stuck until reboot\n",
+				res->data);
+			return -EPROTO;
+		}
 
 		id = res->data;
 
@@ -2209,8 +2219,12 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_service_listeners(struct qcom_scm_qseecom_resp *res)
 			dev_err(__scm->dev,
 				"qseecom: listener %u will not settle, failing it\n",
 				id);
-			qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_respond(id,
+			ret = qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_respond(id,
 					QSEECOM_LISTENER_FAILURE, res);
+			if (ret)
+				dev_err(__scm->dev,
+					"qseecom: could not fail listener %u (%d); the application stays parked and the interface is stuck until reboot\n",
+					id, ret);
 			return -ELOOP;
 		}
 
